{"activity_text": "Antiviral, Anti-HIV", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "The core sequence prior to modification is 65% similar to LabyA2. Chemical modification: LabyA1 contains a special amino acid labionin at positions 1, 4, 8, 10, 13, and 19. Labs 1,4 and labs 10, 13 are connected via a carbon-carbon bond, while labs 4, 8 and labs 13, 19 form normal thioether bonds. In addition, a disulfide bond occurs between C9 and C20. Activity: It inhibited HIV-1 (IC50 1.7 uM), HIV-2 (IC50 1.9 uM), HSV-1 (IC50 0.6 uM), HSV-2 (IC50 0.3 uM). labyrinthopeptins A1, the prototype congeners of carbacyclic lanthipeptides, inhibits the proliferation of diverse enveloped viruses, including dengue virus DENV-2 (IC50 0.55 uM), Zika virus (ZIKV, IC50 0.51-0.99 uM), West Nile virus (WNV IC50 0.2 uM), hepatitis C virus (HCV IC50 1.1 uM), chikungunya virus (CHIKV, IC50 2.2 uM), Kaposi’s sarcoma-associated herpesvirus, cytomegalovirus, and herpes simplex virus, in the low micromolar to nanomolar range ( Hans Prochnow et al., 2020). Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "23724015", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2013 May 28;8(5):e64010. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02526", "source_id": "AP02526", "source_numeric_id": "02526", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02526", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The lantibiotic peptide labyrinthopeptin A1 demonstrates broad anti-HIV and anti-HSV activity with potential for microbicidal applications.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
